 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 11424,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"6139\" data-start=\"6062\">Tkinter widgets allow structured user interaction. For example:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"6231\" data-start=\"6140\">\n\t<li data-end=\"6169\" data-start=\"6140\">\n\t<p data-end=\"6169\" data-start=\"6142\"><code data-end=\"6149\" data-start=\"6142\">Label</code> &ndash; shows static text</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"6201\" data-start=\"6170\">\n\t<p data-end=\"6201\" data-start=\"6172\"><code data-end=\"6179\" data-start=\"6172\">Entry</code> &ndash; receives text input</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"6231\" data-start=\"6202\">\n\t<p data-end=\"6231\" data-start=\"6204\"><code data-end=\"6212\" data-start=\"6204\">Button</code> &ndash; triggers actions</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"6231\" data-start=\"6202\">\n\t<p>from tkinter import *</p>\n\n\t<p>def greet():<br />\n\t&nbsp; &nbsp; name = entry.get()<br />\n\t&nbsp; &nbsp; label.config(text=f&quot;Hello, {name}!&quot;)</p>\n\n\t<p>window = Tk()<br />\n\tentry = Entry(window)<br />\n\tentry.pack()<br />\n\tButton(window, text=&quot;Submit&quot;, command=greet).pack()<br />\n\tlabel = Label(window, text=&quot;&quot;)<br />\n\tlabel.pack()<br />\n\twindow.mainloop()<br />\n\t&nbsp;</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"6231\" data-start=\"6202\">\n\t<p>This form collects input and responds dynamically. Analyzing widget roles helps in designing intuitive UIs.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
